{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway","id":293843,"title":"So just what is GamerGate anyway?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-27T10:04:39-07:00","id":293843,"title":"So just what is GamerGate anyway?","content":"This is one that has managed to go completely over my head for the longest time. Not really on purpose, either, but I suppose I wasn't attentive when it started and thus missed some important context on how it all played out. Afterwards, I probably mentally blocked it out on account of not having the energy to investigate enough to form my own opinion. By now, though, I've kind of gathered that it will have some lasting impact on gaming culture and journalism and the idea of games as an art form, which I <i>am</i> interested in, so I should probably get up to date. Also, I hope that after the critical events have all played out and there's some distance to them, overviewing the process might be easier.<br /> <br /> I've read the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamergate_controversy\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia article</a>, which I hope has given me a grasp on the unfolding of events at least. Does anyone know of any other resource they find useful? I realize most will be biased, but as long as I know that I should be fine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:18:29-07:00","id":293861,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/blog/5-things-i-learned-as-internets-most-hated-person/\" target=\"_blank\">How about something from somebody right in the middle of it all?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T10:39:23-07:00","id":293897,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm rather into games, but have not even noticed whole storm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:02:14-07:00","id":293910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway#post293843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one that has managed to go completely over my head for the longest time. Not really on purpose, either, but I suppose I wasn't attentive when it started and thus missed some important context on how it all played out. Afterwards, I probably mentally blocked it out on account of not having the energy to investigate enough to form my own opinion. By now, though, I've kind of gathered that it will have some lasting impact on gaming culture and journalism and the idea of games as an art form, which I <i>am</i> interested in, so I should probably get up to date. Also, I hope that after the critical events have all played out and there's some distance to them, overviewing the process might be easier.<br /> <br /> I've read the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamergate_controversy\" target=\"_blank\">Wikipedia article</a>, which I hope has given me a grasp on the unfolding of events at least. Does anyone know of any other resource they find useful? I realize most will be biased, but as long as I know that I should be fine.</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?739295-GamerGate-Gamer-Gate-General-Thread-READ-THE-FIRST-POST\" target=\"_blank\">RPGnet thread</a> covers the anti-Gater view of the debate. This is admittedly biased, on the basis that RPGnet's mods regard Gamergaters as a hate group, and if you support what RPGnet holds to be a hate group (which they list and post explanations of their position, with big friendly links), you will be banned. So yeah, the only people voicing their opinion are the skeletons (anti-Gamergaters; name comes from someone finally getting fed up with Social Justice Warrior being used to describe anyone who spoke out against hate speech at all that they find-replaced that term with, well, skeleton).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> ...Being a skeleton myself, here's my personal opinion:<br /> <br /> The result of a rather bitter ex-boyfriend posting a drunken (note:alchohol may or may not have been involved, but it's the same principle) rant about his former beau online. His former beau,is an indie game designer named Zoe Quinn, and part of his slurring anger involved her trading sexual favors for good ratings. You know, sort of like what every dumped boyfriend claims about their ex when he calls her a [gendered sex-related insult].<br /> <br /> This unintentionally gave the embittered hateful basement-dwelling troll part of gamer culture a seemingly legitimate platform to rant about &quot;corruption in games journalism&quot; (ie, the fact that video games being accepted as a wider culture means they have to deal with the fact they can't ignore female gamers with independent identities anymore, with a side of good-ol'-fashioned misogyny). Noted idiot Alec Baldwin (the actor from Firefly-ironic, given Joss Whedon is the most skeletal of skeletons and has been for a long time) gave them their name today, and it stuck.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, my opinion? It's raw reactionary sentiment wrapped in &quot;journalistic ethics&quot; that have more to do with Quinn's entirely personal love life, not to mention taking the rant of a depressed drunk at face value because it was convenient.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:14:37-07:00","id":293932,"title":"","content":"Gamergate as a topic has a tendency to be explosive. Let's try and all be decent to each other here.<br /> <br /> If things <i>do</i> get explosive, we'll probably have to cut off the discussion.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:19:36-07:00","id":293937,"title":"","content":"Go sharpen the knife and get the torch lit, Rose, because I'm sure it won't be long before this hydra needs it's heads cut off.....sadly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:24:17-07:00","id":293943,"title":"","content":"If it involves Social Justice Warriors, then good I &quot;missed&quot; it because I have allergy to them. And I'm right winger so I'm probably among what they think are their sworn enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:35:53-07:00","id":293960,"title":"","content":"I don't have a dog in the whole GamerGate controversy - I don't really play video games much these days, but I find it fascinating.<br /> <br /> It's a wonderful example of how a small minority, thanks to the power and anonymity of the internet, can radically reshape and rebrand a larger message. In all likelihood, the number of &quot;assholes&quot; (the people sending death threats, doxxing, etc) is comparatively small - a few thousand trolls who get off on seeing themselves, or at least their actions, get discussed in online forums, or in news columns. Yet, despite the small number, they've completely taken control of the GamerGate movement, and indeed, in many respects are becoming the face of &quot;male video game players.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think GamerGate started off with, at least in theory, some points that merited discussion involving the integrity if video game journalism(it's no secret that the video game companies that spend the most on advertising in magazines tend to receive best scores for their games, for example), but certainly by now any earlier merits to the movement have been totally eclipsed by the assholes whose actions have painted male gamers in such a negative light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-27-2014, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T11:43:24-07:00","id":293965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=293910#post293910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?739295-GamerGate-Gamer-Gate-General-Thread-READ-THE-FIRST-POST\" target=\"_blank\">RPGnet thread</a> covers the anti-Gater view of the debate. This is admittedly biased, on the basis that RPGnet's mods regard Gamergaters as a hate group, and if you support what RPGnet holds to be a hate group</div> </div> </div> </div>The Southern Poverty Law Center is now tracking #gamergate as a hate group. It's a less extreme position than it sounds like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:00:17-07:00","id":293992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=293965#post293965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Southern Poverty Law Center is now tracking #gamergate as a hate group. It's a less extreme position than it sounds like.</div> </div> </div> </div>You keep on saying this. Searching the SPLC the only thing I can find is a blog link to an article in the guardian that they thew in their misc blog pile.<br /> <br /> This makes gamergate as much of a hate group as Columbus, the north carolina state government or Arizona ballot counters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:25:50-07:00","id":294031,"title":"","content":"Having looked into it a little bit more (and thanks for the link, Papa Bear), I'm starting to get a feeling that I might have attributed the discussion too much credit. From where I currently stand, it really looks a lot more like the usual kind of sexist bullshit than I had at first assumed.<br /> <br /> I do think there's something to be said for having a discussion about video game journalism transparency and interindustrial relations, that can't be a bad thing. But that discussion can't be had while associated with GamerGate, because there's so much wrong going on under that label that it would overshadow everything.<br /> <br /> First of all, of course, the harassment. I mean, you don't have to be any kind of social justice warrior to realize that's not a valid mode of discussion, not if you were really looking to address any issues. This is rule by fear. I saw someone call it terrorism, and I would agree.<br /> <br /> Secondly, the misogyny. Even from the very start, there's an androcentric perspective being produced. The as far as I gather disproven accusation against Quinn is that she slept with Grayson in exchange for a good review (the Wikipedia page says Grayson never reviewed her game). The accusation could have equally easily been that Grayson agreed to trade a good review for a lay. The rhetoric here is clear; despite the implicitly reciprocal nature of both a sexual act and a trade of services, the woman is foregrounded as the one responsible, while the man is never questioned. The same pattern can be seen in, for example, victim blaming in rape situations. The whole premise of the accusation is misogynist from the start, and naturally, the proceeded harassment of multiple female personalities only makes this more obvious. I couldn't help but smile at the tragedy of it all when Sarkeesian got pulled into it again, kind of just because.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, the reactionary stance taken to video games as an art form. The GamerGate supporters seem to represent the opinion that video games should not be examined in a social context, but only in terms of their form (mechanics, controls, graphics and so on) and compared against a certain number of given &quot;golden ideals&quot;, essentially like it is today. I believe that video games is an art form, and if so, to gain credibility they must be examined in the same way we examine our other art: socially, absolutely, but also formally (in that case, not compared to a set of &quot;golden ideals&quot;) and in relation to the individual player. A new academic field? In time, I hope so. Not so the GamerGate advocates, it would seem.<br /> <br /> In that light, I have a feeling I might agree with the &quot;death of the gamer&quot; articles I've read about. I'll have to read them in their entirety myself, but there is something to be said for a term starting to lose its meaning once it gets applied to too many obviously non-homogenous elements.<br /> <br /> I gather that the general opinion all lean the same way here, but does anyone know of any side which may produce a counterargument? Any link to their main hunting grounds, so I can see it firsthand?<br /> <br /> Oh, and in the same vein, on a sidenote: the term &quot;social justice warrior&quot; is a non-defined term, as I've ranted about earlier on these boards. It gets applied so broadly that it really carries no meaning beyond its negative charge. The views of people who get called it, I've come to experience, are often very moderate in their opinions and they are often more about common sense than anything more drastic. Beyond that, social justice seems like a great idea; why would we not want that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-27-2014, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:35:50-07:00","id":294039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Beyond that, social justice seems like a great idea; why would we not want that? </div> </div> </div>The thing is that what one group views as a justice and another group views as a justice may be a different thing. Reaching a consensus in that matter seems to be impossible, even within similar demographics. I'm part of LGBT demographics for example, but I can attest there is no one consensus within the group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T12:49:29-07:00","id":294052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294039#post294039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that what one group views as a justice and another group views as a justice may be a different thing. Reaching a consensus in that matter seems to be impossible, even within similar demographics. I'm part of LGBT demographics for example, but I can attest there is no one consensus within the group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but the term is empty anyway except for its negative charge. It just kind of boggles my mind that someone thought &quot;justice&quot; was a good word to charge negatively.<br /> <br /> Naturally, saying &quot;let's have some social justice up in here!&quot; is vague to the point of uselessness. That's why it's a crappy term if you're looking to actually discuss anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:23:32-07:00","id":294082,"title":"","content":"SJW rage primarily comes from the reference to the tumbler activists, and to a lesser extent the (to some people) overreaching of social justice actions, such as making it legally impossible on some university campuses for anyone visibly caucasian to be a victim of racial hatred or discrimination because... as a white person they are automatically in a superior position. On tumblr of course it can get a little more extreme. If you speak any of the languages of china and are not chinese you get screamed at for cultural appropriation, if you're white you can offer nothing to discussion on reducing class separation because you are privileged, if you're male you're a supporter/benefit from the patriarchy and you are strictly forbidden from voicing an opinion on any LGBT issue if you are hetrosexual. <br /> <br /> Most people tend to ignore that section of the world, but that's where the SJW hate is coming from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That aside, yea, the core people of gamergate are misogynistic assholes. There's a lot of people that are following it under the flag of being about gaming journalism, and there are a lot of people doing genuine good on both sides. Unfortunately while the pro-gamergate side is widely in the lead in quantity, both sides have been using Doxxing, death threats, misrepresentation and generally being insulting to each other as the standard, so I don't see it settling down. The simple fact that it's currently a source of profit pretty much ensures that, but more realistically I don't see it calming down until/unless specific people are identified as the sources of the criminal level death threats and people stop treating &quot;everyone gamergate&quot; and &quot;everyone against gamergate&quot; as the perpetrators and the groups as coordinated entities instead of the chaotic mobs that they are.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:52:44-07:00","id":294106,"title":"","content":"GamerGate is a hashtag movement that has absolutely no leadership, no codified goals, and no approved methodology for achieving those goals, so it quite literally is whatever anyone wants to say it is. As far as I'm concerned, it's a hate movement born when a jilted boyfriend accused his girlfriend of cheating on him and whoring herself to get good reviews for a video game she made (though those last accusations are verifiably untrue); as far as most of its supporters are concerned, it's a movement for journalistic integrity, though I personally have not met the supporter who can give me specific examples of whose journalistic integrity needs correction and how. But seriously, though, it is whatever you want it to be. If the movement refuses to define itself in order to dodge responsibility, then it's anything and everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T13:56:29-07:00","id":294112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294082#post294082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SJW rage primarily comes from the reference to the tumbler activists, and to a lesser extent the (to some people) overreaching of social justice actions, such as making it legally impossible on some university campuses for anyone visibly caucasian to be a victim of racial hatred or discrimination because... as a white person they are automatically in a superior position. On tumblr of course it can get a little more extreme. If you speak any of the languages of china and are not chinese you get screamed at for cultural appropriation, if you're white you can offer nothing to discussion on reducing class separation because you are privileged, if you're male you're a supporter/benefit from the patriarchy and you are strictly forbidden from voicing an opinion on any LGBT issue if you are hetrosexual.<br /> <br /> Most people tend to ignore that section of the world, but that's where the SJW hate is coming from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaaha. I must admit I didn't know about that background for the term. Possibly on account of not having a Tumblr account. I should have conducted better research before forming my opinion on it, though, and I can now see where the negative charge comes from. Thanks for that, Canuck.<br /> <br /> As I have seen it applied, though, I still contend it's a silly term.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T14:50:04-07:00","id":294168,"title":"","content":"I've not researched the gamersgate thing at all. I don't really care about it. But there has been a corruption of journalistic integrity involving video games. I'm not talking about the alegations that she slept her way up the ranks. I'm talking about money and corporations. Most of the advertisments on game review sites and the few magazines that survive are filled with ads for the games they are reviewing from the companies. They are often forced to give games that get terrible reviews from gamers fantastic scores at the threat of losing their ad revenue. I'm talking about things like the fact that many of these publications (kotaku, polygon, game informer) brushed aside the always online shitstorm as butthurt angry&quot;man-children&quot; gamers who should get with the times, changing of game scores (Polygon and IGN are both guilty of this. Removed old reviews and replaced them with better ones).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>pls respont","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/372-cerealkiller","name":"cerealkiller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar372_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T15:34:51-07:00","id":294196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cerealkiller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294168#post294168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not researched the gamersgate thing at all. I don't really care about it. But there has been a corruption of journalistic integrity involving video games. I'm not talking about the alegations that she slept her way up the ranks. I'm talking about money and corporations. Most of the advertisments on game review sites and the few magazines that survive are filled with ads for the games they are reviewing from the companies. They are often forced to give games that get terrible reviews from gamers fantastic scores at the threat of losing their ad revenue. I'm talking about things like the fact that many of these publications (kotaku, polygon, game informer) brushed aside the always online shitstorm as butthurt angry&quot;man-children&quot; gamers who should get with the times, changing of game scores (Polygon and IGN are both guilty of this. Removed old reviews and replaced them with better ones).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, that's kinda why it's something of a red herring to me. Games and reviews have been hand in hand in computer games since the 70's.<br /> <br /> Not that there isn't a legitimate reason to not want that to be the state of affairs, it's just not a new one. And frankly I think the industry is still too small to support any sort of extensive separation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T19:22:18-07:00","id":294419,"title":"","content":"Gamergate is pretty much gamer culture's extinction burst. My favorite quote on the subject:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">It's hilarious because these people, the harassers, are fighting a completely losing battle and the spasms of hatred really are more like the twitches of a dying body than a coordinated response. They are suddenly out of their depth in a world they thought was created entirely for them, a masturbatory fantasy land they think they &quot;own&quot; because, apparently, women in gaming is a &quot;new thing&quot;.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">These people are on the wrong side of history, and they have spent their lives consuming only one media form, one that has largely been exempt from any real criticism in the past. Gaming has been niche, and niche cultural expressions are not necessarily judged in a similar way to more established ones. Misogyny in gaming has been handwaved away by the rest of the world as &quot;games are for children and manchildren&quot;.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">Now, games are faced with the same criticism and intellectual discussion as other forms of media. These crazy things called &quot;books&quot; and &quot;films&quot; have feminist (and other -ist) critiques which add to the understanding of what it means to say something in the cultural arena. BROGAMERS and their ilk literally cannot understand why this is happening to games. They cannot, and will not separate &quot;critical analysis&quot; from &quot;criticism&quot;. Some of the best literature has gone through decades (if not, sometimes, thousands of years) of deconstruction, discussion and rewriting. People search for intended and subverted meaning, suggest death-of-the-author interpretations and even rehouse the story in their own cultural understanding just to tell it in a slightly different way.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#444444\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">You can take the Odyssey and say &quot;No, Penelope's experiences are just as important as Odysseus's&quot; and you've made a valuable contribution to the world of books. But, christ, you say &quot;hey maybe having sexy corpses of prostitutes everywhere for the player to try and get a look up their skirt is a bit sexist&quot; and a legion of man-children will claw their way out of their mother's basement, brush doritos dust off their wanking hand and start doxxing you.</span></span> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T22:57:34-07:00","id":294546,"title":"","content":"So I spotted some statements from TotalBiscuit on the issue. First <a href=\"https://twitter.com/Totalbiscuit/status/520242699082145792\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and then <a href=\"http://blueplz.blogspot.co.uk/2014/10/whose-side-am-i-on.html\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. In summary, he's taking a middle stance, condemning the harassment from both sides and asking the GamerGate people to show their hand and actually talk journalism ethics.<br /> <br /> He makes some statements I don't agree with, like suggesting that reciprocating with the GamerGate harassers has only &quot;fuelled the fire&quot; and allowed it to continue; while this may be true, I think it's more important to speak up about what kind of thing happen to people, on the internet and otherwise, who deal with these subjects. I'm also not sure it's more important to talk ethics than to actually help those getting harassed, but it seems TB thinks the one will bring about the other. I'm skeptical, but I suppose we have different outlooks.<br /> <br /> I'll not deny I watch TB, mostly because he's a good caster and like hearing his voice (it's not creepy &gt;.&gt;). He's opinionated, but mostly factual and has an ability to keep two thoughts running at once. I don't think he'd ever call himself a feminist, but he does support women in gaming and has an anti-harassment stance. He's just not very active about it. More like he's not standing in their way. Much as I lament it, it's not strange that he'd take this stance; he's very much a &quot;mechanics-guy&quot; and I can see him sympathizing, if not with the brogamer attitude or the oppression of females, then with the idea that mainstream art criticism isn't interesting for games.<br /> <br /> TB's views on these things have always been kind of iffy for me. He tends to be able to argue them down to a level where it's hard to disagree with the things he <i>does</i> say, but often feel there are further implications that should maybe get more consideration. For example, I personally agree, as I've said above, that journalistic ethics in the games medium is a valid discussion topic, and I don't think it's wrong to discuss it with GamerGate-associated people - we shouldn't be &quot;afraid to touch&quot;. Putting them to task might be a the best thing we can do; let them prove that it actually <i>is</i> about ethics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294419#post294419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gamergate is pretty much gamer culture's extinction burst.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm personally of the opinion that such an extended criticism of games would be a wonderful thing to experience in my lifetime, but I don't think this is the last stand of the brogamers, or even that they will go away. An academic criticism of games will probably coexist with a commercial one, just like for most other media today. The anti-feminist sentiments are strong in the gaming culture, but they are not a product of it; the problem is present in our culture at large.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 10-28-2014, 02:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T23:50:53-07:00","id":294559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294419#post294419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gamergate is pretty much gamer culture's extinction burst. My favorite quote on the subject:</div> </div> </div> </div>Your quote would be a lot better if it didn't end up implying that gamers who do enjoy those sorts of games, are fat, dorito-chomping man-children who live in basements and such. It's one of the problems that you often see in this sort of debate - people are often less interested in trying to make a point, and a little more eager to throw out a zinger to get &quot;the other side.&quot; <br /> <br /> Realistically though, games like Grand Theft Auto are big, big bucks. GTA 4 sold over 25 million copies - that's a lot of money. As long as &quot;Brogamers&quot; are willing to drop hundreds of millions of dollars on a game, there will always be games made to cater to them.<br /> <br /> Ideally you'll end up with games that appeal to everyone - you'll have games for X group or games for Y group (sort of like how with books, you have so many different types, from fantasy to history to politics, etc). <br /> <br /> I think the issue is, with many people among the GamerGate crowd, that they see a desire to force these changes on gaming, rather than have them happen naturally. So rather than having new games come out that appeal to audiences other than the &quot;traditional gamer crowd,&quot; they feel that there is a movement that seeks to pressure manufactures to produce games that appeal to non-traditional gamers, at the expense of games that appeal to the traditional gamer crowd. <br /> <br /> It would be sort of like, if there was a group of people pushing fantasy novel publishers/authors to include science-fiction elements in their books. So you end up with fantasy authors sticking light sabers and laser guns in their otherwise fantasy settings in order to appeal to this other group of people. It's understandable if traditional fantasy fans took umbrage with that - &quot;If you like fantasy/science fiction so much, why not support new authors and new publishers who cater to that, rather than forcing existing ones to change in order to appeal to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> And, I can understand the general sentiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T00:29:31-07:00","id":294595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294559#post294559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your quote would be a lot better if it didn't end up implying that gamers who do enjoy those sorts of games, are fat, dorito-chomping man-children who live in basements and such. It's one of the problems that you often see in this sort of debate - people are often less interested in trying to make a point, and a little more eager to throw out a zinger to get &quot;the other side.&quot;<br /> <br /> Realistically though, games like Grand Theft Auto are big, big bucks. GTA 4 sold over 25 million copies - that's a lot of money. As long as &quot;Brogamers&quot; are willing to drop hundreds of millions of dollars on a game, there will always be games made to cater to them.<br /> <br /> Ideally you'll end up with games that appeal to everyone - you'll have games for X group or games for Y group (sort of like how with books, you have so many different types, from fantasy to history to politics, etc).<br /> <br /> I think the issue is, with many people among the GamerGate crowd, that they see a desire to force these changes on gaming, rather than have them happen naturally. So rather than having new games come out that appeal to audiences other than the &quot;traditional gamer crowd,&quot; they feel that there is a movement that seeks to pressure manufactures to produce games that appeal to non-traditional gamers, at the expense of games that appeal to the traditional gamer crowd.<br /> <br /> It would be sort of like, if there was a group of people pushing fantasy novel publishers/authors to include science-fiction elements in their books. So you end up with fantasy authors sticking light sabers and laser guns in their otherwise fantasy settings in order to appeal to this other group of people. It's understandable if traditional fantasy fans took umbrage with that - &quot;If you like fantasy/science fiction so much, why not support new authors and new publishers who cater to that, rather than forcing existing ones to change in order to appeal to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> And, I can understand the general sentiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you mix up having games that appeal to everyone and having a criticism of games that take into account other aspects than those it does today. The suggested solution of having games for all people to enjoy still limits the medium to being about enjoyment, about deriving its primary value from how entertaining it is. I contend that there is more to be had from games than this, that they can serve to tell us about our society, touch their consumers on a personal level and affect people in the same way other art forms do. What the current hardcore gaming culture seems to argue is that there is no value in these questions, but that the proper way to judge a game is by a list of established variables alone. I would say that this evaluation mostly measures how well <i>crafted</i> the game is. Opening up the critical field would do loads to promote video games as an art form as well, instead of just a source of entertainment. It would be the difference between judging how closely someone managed to write an article in a consistent and legible handwriting and judging the points in the text they have written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T01:15:34-07:00","id":294612,"title":"","content":"Ah, video games as art vs video games as entertainment...<br /> <br /> Personally I think that video games are first and foremost a form of <i>entertainment</i> - thus the word game.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that you can't have a game that <i>also</i> teaches you think, or causes you to reflect on the world or whatever, but ultimately games are about being entertained (whether having fun, getting scared or having some other emotional reaction).<br /> <br /> Certainly it's possible to have an electronic media that doesn't focus on entertainment and instead on say, teaching or some such. For example, virtual tours of ancient buildings or such aren't really &quot;games.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ultimately though I think that if you're playing a game and aren't entertained then, as a game, the product is clearly a failure, even if it's a critical success on some sort of abstract artistic or social level.<br /> <br /> So I would argue that, when making a video game the priority is (or should be) based on entertaining the people who will play it. And if the priority <i>isn't</i> on entertaining people, then you shouldn't call what you're making a <i>game.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-28-2014, 06:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T05:40:04-07:00","id":294727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294559#post294559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your quote would be a lot better if it didn't end up implying that gamers who do enjoy those sorts of games, are fat, Dorito-chomping man-children who live in basements and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't, though. The first line of the quote specifically calls out harassers. I think it's pretty clear what kind of gamer the author is referring to.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T06:00:22-07:00","id":294739,"title":"","content":"Gamergate is a couples spat turned into some sort of ideological death battle that in the end is completely meaningless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Do the dead dare walk the Earth before my eyes? Will the undead raise an army, fall in, and advance? Will those who would abandon God and embrace the heretical order DARE to presume to meet my gaze!? Iscariot will not allow it. <b>I</b> will not allow it.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3889-ninjasantaclause","name":"Ninjasantaclause","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T08:10:05-07:00","id":294835,"title":"","content":"But I thought we didn't <i>need</i> feminism anymore?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T08:11:28-07:00","id":294838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294082#post294082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">both sides have been using Doxxing, death threats</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Citation needed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T11:22:54-07:00","id":295017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294838#post294838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Citation needed.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.gamezone.com/originals/the-dangers-and-ramifications-of-doxxing-and-swatting\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://gamezone.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/GZ_logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.gamezone.com/originals/the-dangers-and-ramifications-of-doxxing-and-swatting\" target=\"_blank\"> GameZone &ndash; GameZone. Built for gamers, by gamers </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.gamezone.com/originals/the-dangers-and-ramifications-of-doxxing-and-swatting\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.gamezone.com/originals/the-dangers-and-ramifications-of-doxxing-and-swatting </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T13:07:40-07:00","id":295116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=295017#post295017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"http://www.gamezone.com/originals/the-dangers-and-ramifications-of-doxxing-and-swatting\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.gamezone.com/originals/th...g-and-swatting</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have anything else? I even read the YouTube comments on the videos from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nHJl3Rd5Uuc\" target=\"_blank\">Kootra</a><span style=\"color:#292929\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">, </span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fQVbM9OuZIs\" target=\"_blank\">Phantomlord</a><span style=\"color:#292929\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">and </span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AQ8T0CZ0sbA\" target=\"_blank\">coL.n0thing</a> and there was no mention of a connection to #GamerGate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T14:48:20-07:00","id":295245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=295116#post295116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have anything else? I even read the YouTube comments on the videos from <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nHJl3Rd5Uuc\" target=\"_blank\">Kootra</a><span style=\"color:#292929\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">, </span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fQVbM9OuZIs\" target=\"_blank\">Phantomlord</a><span style=\"color:#292929\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica Neue\">and </span></span><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AQ8T0CZ0sbA\" target=\"_blank\">coL.n0thing</a> and there was no mention of a connection to #GamerGate.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> Well, we can go the route of assuming that when one of the major figures leading a group/mob/thing get doxxed and threats mailed to them that it has absolutely nothing to do with that group/mob/thing. It is indeed completely possible that it is unrelated due to the lack of a direct tie of any sort, entirely possible it was just someone else with an old grudge sending the threat. The note included was rather generic of just &quot;Kill Yourself&quot; and the needle sent along was without a note as I understand it.<br /> <br /> However if that is the basis we're going to go on for evaluation criteria it should be applied equally don't you think? So anything attributed to attacks by Gamergate, such as the email threat causing the cancellation of the Utah presentation should be discounted as a gamergate related threat since it in no way mentioned gamergate.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T14:49:00-07:00","id":295246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294559#post294559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your quote would be a lot better if it didn't end up implying that gamers who do enjoy those sorts of games, are fat, dorito-chomping man-children who live in basements and such. It's one of the problems that you often see in this sort of debate - people are often less interested in trying to make a point, and a little more eager to throw out a zinger to get &quot;the other side.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The point is, if you wrap a disproportionate amount of your identity into one consumer-driven activity (e.g. playing video games) and the industry built around that activity has, for a long time, viewed your demographic as themes important one to appeal to for profit (for a long time this has primarily been male children, teens, and young adults), then it makes sense when your demographic seems to matter less to the industry, because the result is an assault on your identity. If the game industry focuses less on games aimed at men versus games with a wider appeal; if the game industry starts to focus more on early-30-somethings than teens (which is happening, because the current crop of late-20s/early-30s people of all genders are the largest games consumers, far above and beyond teens); if the game industry starts to look at portrayals of minorities in games and decides that hewing to stereotypical depictions of women and ethnic minorities might cost them more money than it earns...then the game industry (which, we must recall, is a for-profit industry) will adjust to maximize its profits.<br /> <br /> That adjustment scares people who were previously part of the target demographic. Playing video games used to be a much &quot;nerdier&quot; thing but the industry has, over time, worked pretty hard to target games at larger audiences (unsurprisingly, because if you mainly appeal to teen boys you're intentionally ignoring huge swathes of the population who might otherwise throw money at you). When you feel like your interest (here defined by your consumption preferences) is being diluted and is no longer recognizable to your nostalgic feelings, and you are so wrapped up int eh identity of &quot;gaming&quot; (and that is the kicker) then it makes sense that responses are going to be angry.<br /> <br /> What I find most hilarious is the whole sudden call to the notion of &quot;ethics in games journalism.&quot; GG has willfully ignored how pretty much all publications will write glowing reviews for shitty games in order to keep reaping the benefits of association (and this has gone on for <i>decades </i>but suddenly it's only mentioned now?) Instead they want to get mad when a woman cheats on her boyfriend with someone in the games journalism industry and they think that's evidence of some kind of corruption, <i>even when the guy she slept with never reviewed the game she produced. </i>There's <i>totally </i>corruption in games journalism, but the Zoe Quinn situation sure ain't an example of it. I don't consider the whole TFYC fiasco to be tied into journalistic ethics either, though I think that's where most of the flak against Quinn comes from (well, the parts that aren't &quot;how dare she cheat on a guy&quot;).<br /> <br /> I don't even know how Aneeta Sarkeesian is supposed to factor in to the whole &quot;ethics in games journalism&quot; thing given she raised money to put out videos discussing sexism in video games. I guess Kickstarting capital and doing this somehow ties into ethics in games journalism or something, or I'm sure someone has definitely spun it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:02:43-07:00","id":295385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=293960#post293960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">certainly by now any earlier merits to the movement have been totally eclipsed by the assholes whose actions have painted male gamers in such a negative light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ohhhh...<br /> <br /> <i>Now</i> I understand what &quot;not all men&quot; means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T17:36:00-07:00","id":295438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/293843-so-just-what-is-gamergate-anyway?p=294559#post294559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\\<br /> I think the issue is, with many people among the GamerGate crowd, that they see a desire to force these changes on gaming, rather than have them happen naturally. So rather than having new games come out that appeal to audiences other than the &quot;traditional gamer crowd,&quot; they feel that there is a movement that seeks to pressure manufactures to produce games that appeal to non-traditional gamers, at the expense of games that appeal to the traditional gamer crowd.<br /> <br /> It would be sort of like, if there was a group of people pushing fantasy novel publishers/authors to include science-fiction elements in their books. So you end up with fantasy authors sticking light sabers and laser guns in their otherwise fantasy settings in order to appeal to this other group of people. It's understandable if traditional fantasy fans took umbrage with that - &quot;If you like fantasy/science fiction so much, why not support new authors and new publishers who cater to that, rather than forcing existing ones to change in order to appeal to you?&quot;<br /> <br /> And, I can understand the general sentiment.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this hilarious.<br /> <br /> I remember reading angry letters to the editor in Isaac Aasimov's Science Fiction Magazine ranting about the rise of fantasy and magic and effects which the author never explains scientifically. So much rage! Reading over 'em again recently, they reminded me a great deal about much of what goes on in online discourse these days. You get a population which sees its taste in media as an important facet of self-identity, and they react to changes in that media as a personal affront. The rise of fantasy authors was an attack on the very nature of science fiction, or it was a decent yarn but you shouldn't include it in a magazine with &quot;real&quot; science fiction, or the author was a lazy or unintelligent hack for including plot elements which aren't explicable by the science of the day. Hard Sci-Fi fans got up in arms even about stories who used too much technobabble but weren't based on actual science.<br /> <br /> This reminds me of that.<br /> <br /> The medium is broadening. The &quot;movement to pressure manufacturers to produce games that appeal to non-traditional gamers&quot; is real! This is an industry! Sci-Fi editors who enjoyed some fantasy in their sci-fi made a conscious choice to allow it in (or to keep allowing it in after the first flames started appearing in their mailboxes), and literature has changed significantly as a result! This isn't bad, this is a medium growing and evolving rather than stagnating! Watching people complain that they're losing something to this movement is ridiculous: there will always be games aimed at their traditional niche, just as there will always be hard sci-fi stories. But I think we'll find that the new stories games are telling will have a broad appeal. This is going to be a good thing for everybody. Harry Potter couldn't have gotten published in the early eighties. A broader medium means you're more likely to get a masterpiece that lights the world on fire and turns everybody into a gamer.<br /> <br /> If you think that's bad, it's because you don't want these other people to be gamers, and if that's the case...well, you've turned your identity politics into self-righteousness and elitism, and I don't care much what you think. Anyone who wants to keep a medium for themselves instead of helping it grow is doing themself and their medium a disservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T20:31:01-07:00","id":295574,"title":"","content":"I am going to be very careful about posting into a thread such as this, but with the whole Gamergate movement, you know which one is in the wrong when the first line of defense from them is to attack with death threats. This shows a willful ignorance into trying to learn the truth, and more towards finding any potential outlet to fuel their hatred and rage against any target that now seems to be validated regardless of cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date"